Chapter: ConstraintPrim
  cites Foreword chapter Console

 Generic Show/Ord constraints work on primitive arguments too: the
 concrete type's builtin show/compare is wrapped as __show_Integer etc
 and threaded as the dictionary, so describe and rel work on Integer,
 Text, and Boolean directly.

Section: Body

  describe : Show a => a -> Text
  describe (x) = "[" & show x & "]"

  rel : Ord a => a -> a -> Text
  rel (x) (y) = if compare x y < 0 then "lt" else "ge"

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    print-line-uni (describe 42)
    print-line-uni (describe "hi")
    print-line-uni (describe True)
    print-line-uni (rel 1 2)
    print-line-uni (rel 5 5)
  end

